{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9tm6WS28WJRtoikjcjt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled F1 **DISMISS not-worth-cost**. The verdict is in `docs/reviews/wi-925/001-ADJUDICATE-20a6044.md`, committed as `7a0f7c323` with the `WI: WI-925` trailer; the commit checks passed and the kit's dispute parser accepts the ruling line.\n\n**The finding is real.** I read the plan's P5 (lines 562–590). Its `_relink_remap` only pairs work-item closes, an `active/<branch>/` delete with a closed-folder add. It leaves out the spec-of-record archive move (`docs/specs/<name>.md` to `docs/archive/specs/`), which `spec_move.py` documents as part of a close. If another claimed row's Done-when linked that spec, the landing would be held.\n\n**It's in scope, but not worth the fix:**\n- **Not contrived.** The archive move is a supported close route, so it isn't out of scope.\n- **It fails closed.** A miss holds the landing rather than letting anything through. The gate's own done-when blessing clears it, so the cost of a miss is one extra sitting.\n- **It has never happened.** None of the 221 work items with a Done-when section links any spec. Not even the parent case the deliverable targets has occurred; the spec itself says it was \"found by reading, not reproduced\", which is why that deliverable starts with a reproduction step.\n- **It's not a Done-when gap.** The relink Done-when item is tied to one fixture (X's work spec closing), and the plan covers it fully. The omission only narrows the deliverable's broader wording, so it isn't the convergence-class gap the reviewer called it, and it opens nothing.\n- **The fix costs more than the defect.** It's a few lines of code, but it widens an exemption to the Done-when hold, and every new pattern there needs its own exact-byte proof. It would also force a revision of a plan already at its cap.\n\n**One thing to be transparent about:** I counted that cap cost as part of the fix's cost. Here only a DISMISS lets the pass record be written, and FIX or SUCCESSOR would send the lane to the owner. I'd still have ruled DISMISS on the defect's weight alone: it fails closed, is recoverable, and has never occurred.\n\n**Advisory, not a condition:** the lane should name this pair as a stated limit rather than leave it silent. A line in deliverable 4's residue list and in LLR-307's bound would do: an archival pair isn't in the relink map, and a Done-when it relinks is held until blessed. If such a link ever shows up, the shared relink stage P4 extracts is where the pair belongs.\n\nThe untracked `.requested` binding file is the coordinator's, and I didn't touch it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":653,"cache_read_input_tokens":831743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":653},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"e82b59a0-7ecc-4f9f-a739-3911349e4b53","timestamp":"2026-10-18T14:53:35.966Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9tm6CpnWQ1kmJFBQMhL"}
